115
00:26:00,469 --> 00:26:07,069
なるようにきつく 結んでいてほしいの
Tying it so they will stay nice and tight...

116
00:26:07,069 --> 00:26:14,569
ほしいの 腕はここに 思い出は遠くに
I want my arms right here, and memories far away...

117
00:26:14,569 --> 00:26:22,269
気づけばそこにある くらいがいい
It's best when you realize it's right there beside you.

118
00:26:24,269 --> 00:26:30,969
黙って引っ張ったりしないでよ 不格好な蝶にしないでよ
Don't pull on it in silence, don't turn it into an ugly butterfly...

119
00:26:30,969 --> 00:26:38,269
結んだつもりがほどいていたり 緩めたつもりが締めていたり
Thinking we tied it when it was coming undone, thinking we loosened it when we were tightening it...

120
00:26:39,369 --> 00:26:46,569
はるかに はるかに
Far, far away...

121
00:27:02,769 --> 00:27:09,869
この蒼くて広い世界に 無数に散らばった中から
Out of countless pieces scattered across this deep blue and wide world...

122
00:27:09,869 --> 00:27:16,569
別々に二人選んだ糸を お互いたぐり寄せ合ったんだ
We chose separate threads and pulled them close to each other.

123
00:27:16,969 --> 00:27:23,269
結ばれたんじゃなく 結んだんだ 二人で 「せーの」 で引っ張ったんだ
We didn't just get tied together; we tied it ourselves, pulling together on the count of three.

124
00:27:23,269 --> 00:27:30,669
大きくも 小さくも なりすぎないように 力を込めたんだ
Putting our strength into it so it wouldn't become too big or too small.

125
00:27:30,669 --> 00:27:37,769
この蒼くて広い世界に 無数に散らばった中から
Out of countless threads scattered across this deep blue and wide world...

126
00:27:37,869 --> 00:27:43,669
別々に二人選んだ糸を お互いたぐり寄せ合ったんだ
We chose separate threads and pulled them close to each other.

127
00:27:43,869 --> 00:27:50,269
結ばれたんじゃなく 結んだんだ 二人で 「せーの」 で引っ張ったんだ
We didn't just get tied together; we tied it ourselves, pulling together on the count of three.

128
00:27:50,269 --> 00:27:57,269
大きくも 小さくも なりすぎないように 力を込めたんだ
Putting our strength into it so it wouldn't become too big or too small.

129
00:28:47,869 --> 00:28:52,869
[Title: 花になって 作詞: 長屋晴子 作曲: 穴見真吾]
[Title: Hana ni Natte Lyrics: Haruko Nagaya Music: Shingo Anami]

130
00:28:58,169 --> 00:29:02,169
陰にそっと隠れようがいいんじゃない?
Isn't it fine to quietly hide in the shadows?

131
00:29:02,869 --> 00:29:07,169
蕾のような花だってあるじゃない
Isn't there a flower like a budding flower?

132
00:29:07,969 --> 00:29:12,169
秘密にして守るのがいいんじゃない
Isn't it good to keep it a secret and protect it?

133
00:29:12,969 --> 00:29:17,869
誰にも邪魔されず 華麗に咲いてる
Blooming splendidly without anyone disturbing you.

134
00:29:18,369 --> 00:29:20,369
甘い苦いにハマんない
Don't get hooked on the sweet and bitter.

135
00:29:20,669 --> 00:29:22,669
その判断がくだんない
That judgment is so pointless.

136
00:29:22,969 --> 00:29:27,169
気に病んで下を向かないでいて
Don't let it weigh on you and look down.

137
00:29:27,969 --> 00:29:32,769
愛に慣れちゃいない 無駄に飾らない
Not used to love, never decorating uselessly.

138
00:29:32,969 --> 00:29:35,269
綺麗にされた花瓶も
Even a prettied-up vase...

139
00:29:35,969 --> 00:29:37,969
肥やしも何もいらない
No fertilizer or anything else is needed.

140
00:29:38,169 --> 00:29:41,769
その姿が美しい
That appearance alone is beautiful.

141
00:29:42,169 --> 00:29:47,769
花になって ほらニヒルに笑って その顔に
Become a flower, look, smile cynically, and on that face...

142
00:29:47,869 --> 00:29:51,869
ぞくぞくして目が離せない 味見して
Thrilling me so I can't take my eyes off you, take a taste.

143
00:29:52,869 --> 00:29:59,369
君の毒は私の薬って包んであげるから
I'll wrap it up saying your poison is my medicine.

144
00:30:00,784 --> 00:30:02,944
笑って
Smile...

145
00:30:07,876 --> 00:30:17,856
ねえ、会いたい会いたい その笑顔に会いたい会いたいって言えば笑ってくれるかな
Hey, I want to see you, I want to see you... If I say I want to see you, will you smile for me?

146
00:30:18,476 --> 00:30:21,376
陰から支えるくらいはいいじゃない
Isn't it fine to support you from the shadows?

147
00:30:23,536 --> 00:30:27,156
欲を言えばこの手で咲かせてみせたい
If I'm being greedy, I want to make it bloom with my own hands.

148
00:30:28,256 --> 00:30:39,996
病のように心を喰らう花枯らしてないのさ
I won't let the flower that devours the heart like a sickness wither away.

149
00:30:40,816 --> 00:30:50,876
光を届かずとも水を上げつづけるから
Even if the light doesn't reach, I'll keep pouring water on it.

150
00:30:53,256 --> 00:31:02,856
いつ陰に気付いて 君は素敵で自惚れでもどう お大事に
When will you notice the shadows? You're wonderful, even if you're full of yourself. Take care.

151
00:31:03,956 --> 00:31:07,596
無自覚なまま愛を蓄えて
Accumulating love unconsciously...

152
00:31:08,516 --> 00:31:10,436
綺麗にされた花瓶も
Even a neatly arranged vase...

153
00:31:10,616 --> 00:31:17,856
肥やしも何もいらない その姿で咲き誇れ
Needs no fertilizer or anything, bloom proudly in that form!

154
00:31:19,936 --> 00:31:28,916
花になって ほらニヒルに笑って その顔にぞくぞくして目が離せない
Become a flower, look, smile nihilistically, I get chills from that face and can't take my eyes off you.

155
00:31:29,556 --> 00:31:38,736
味見して 君の毒は私の薬って包んであげるから
Taste it, I'll wrap your poison in my medicine.

156
00:31:39,576 --> 00:31:48,216
楽にして 君の闇を私の光で愛してあげるから
Make yourself at ease, I'll love your darkness with my light.

157
00:31:48,476 --> 00:31:50,156
笑って
Smile...

158
00:32:13,678 --> 00:32:15,678
[Title: ドライフラワー]
[Title: Dried Flower]

159
00:32:23,840 --> 00:32:34,700
多分、私じゃなくていいね 余裕のない二人だったし 気付けば喧嘩ばっかりしてさ ごめんね
Probably it's fine that it wasn't me, we were two people without any leeway, and before I knew it we were always fighting, sorry.

160
00:32:36,320 --> 00:32:47,920
ずっと話そうと思ってた きっと私たち合わないね 二人きりしかいない部屋でさ 貴方ばかり話していたよね
I'd been thinking of talking about it for a long time, surely we aren't a match, in a room where it was just the two of us, you were always the only one talking.

161
00:32:49,280 --> 00:33:00,700
もしいつか何処かで会えたら 今日の事を笑ってくれるかな
If someday we happen to meet somewhere, I wonder if you'll laugh about today.

162
00:33:01,840 --> 00:33:14,120
理由もちゃんと話せないけれど 貴方が眠った後に泣くのは嫌 声も顔も不器用なとこも全部全部 嫌いじゃないの
Even though I can't explain the reason properly, crying after you've fallen asleep is no good, neither your voice, your face, nor your clumsy parts—I don't hate any of it at all.

163
00:33:15,120 --> 00:33:26,900
ドライフラワーみたい 君との日々も きっときっときっときっと 色褪せる
Like a dried flower, my days with you too will surely, surely, surely, surely fade.

164
00:33:27,920 --> 00:33:37,960
ドライフラワーみたい 君との日々も きっときっときっときっと 色褪せる
Like a dried flower, our days too will surely, surely, surely, surely fade.

165
00:33:38,720 --> 00:33:42,300
色褪せる
Fade.

166
00:33:57,640 --> 00:34:09,300
多分、君じゃなくてよかった もう泣かされることもないし 「私ばかり」なんて言葉も なくなった
Probably it was good that it wasn't you, I don't get made to cry anymore, and words like 'always me' are gone too.

167
00:34:10,300 --> 00:34:18,960
あんなに悲しい別れでも 時間が経てば忘れてく 新しい人と並ぶ君は ちゃんとうまくやれているのかな
Even such a sad farewell, time makes you forget, I wonder if you are doing well standing beside someone new.

168
00:34:22,620 --> 00:34:34,580
もう顔も見たくないからさ 変に連絡してこないでほしい
I don't want to see your face anymore, so please don't reach out strangely.

169
00:34:35,340 --> 00:34:47,840
都合がいいのは変わってないんだね でも無視できずにまた少し返事
You haven't changed, always so convenient, but unable to ignore it, I reply a little again.

170
00:34:48,420 --> 00:35:00,520
多分今も 嫌いじゃないの
Probably even now... I don't hate it.

171
00:35:02,237 --> 00:35:05,377
声も顔も不器用なとこも
Even the clumsy parts of your voice and face,

172
00:35:05,617 --> 00:35:07,477
全部 全部
everything, everything...

173
00:35:08,097 --> 00:35:12,557
きっと きっと きっと きっと きっと
Surely, surely, surely, surely, surely...

174
00:35:12,957 --> 00:35:19,037
色褪せる
fading away...

175
00:35:28,557 --> 00:35:33,957
月灯りに魔物が揺れる きっと私もどうかしてる
Spirits sway in the moonlight, surely I must be losing my mind too.

176
00:35:34,457 --> 00:35:39,437
暗闇に色彩が浮かぶ
Colors emerge in the darkness.

177
00:35:41,657 --> 00:35:47,277
赤黄藍色が胸の奥 ずっと貴方の名前を呼ぶ
Red, yellow, and indigo colors deep in my chest, I keep calling your name.

178
00:35:47,617 --> 00:35:52,277
好きという気持ちまた香る
The feeling of love scents the air once more.

179
00:35:53,277 --> 00:36:05,837
声も顔も不器用なとこも 全部 全部 全部 大嫌いだよ
Even the clumsy parts of your voice and face, I hate everything, everything, everything about you!

180
00:36:06,097 --> 00:36:12,117
まだ枯れない花を 君に添えてさ
Offering you a flower that still hasn't withered,

181
00:36:13,197 --> 00:36:20,377
ずっと ずっと ずっと ずっと 抱えてよ
hold onto it forever, and ever, and ever, and ever.

182
00:37:17,494 --> 00:37:22,754
「大丈夫」と また嘘をついた
"I'm fine," I lied once again,

183
00:37:23,394 --> 00:37:29,754
無理してるの 声でわかるよ
You're pushing yourself, I can tell by your voice.

184
00:37:31,054 --> 00:37:39,774
無理してるの 声でわかるよ バレてるんだよ
You're pushing yourself, I can tell by your voice, you can see right through it.

185
00:37:50,834 --> 00:37:56,634
見た目だとか 性格だって違うあなた
You're someone whose appearance and personality are different from mine,

186
00:37:56,994 --> 00:38:02,634
だけど似てるとこも 意外とあって 共鳴すぐにしたんだ
you're surprisingly similar in some ways, and we resonated instantly.

187
00:38:03,334 --> 00:38:09,094
惹かれ合った私たち
We were drawn to each other,

188
00:38:09,354 --> 00:38:15,874
不思議なこの絆 なんだかさ寝れなくて
this mysterious bond... somehow I couldn't sleep.

189
00:38:16,294 --> 00:38:22,174
夢を語り明かそう 私がね 頑張れる理由
Let's talk about our dreams until morning—the reason why I can do my best...

190
00:38:22,934 --> 00:38:28,314
そう 一人じゃないから
That's right, because I'm not alone.

191
00:38:28,534 --> 00:38:34,374
あなたが笑えば 私もつられる
Whenever you smile, I get drawn in too.

192
00:38:35,214 --> 00:38:41,954
隣り合わせの心 連鎖してるよ
Our side-by-side hearts are creating a chain reaction.

193
00:38:42,194 --> 00:38:48,294
時には歩幅が ずれてしまうけど
Sometimes our paces might fall out of sync,

194
00:38:48,534 --> 00:38:56,434
二人 呼吸 揃え さあ 未来へと 進んで行こう
two of us matching our breathing, come on, let's advance into the future.

195
00:38:58,234 --> 00:39:03,274
どれくらいの順位かな 周りと比べて
What's our ranking like compared to those around us?

196
00:39:03,854 --> 00:39:09,734
果てしないトラック 先頭追いつけるの？
Can we catch up to the front of this endless track?

197
00:39:10,534 --> 00:39:16,194
なんて 弱気な日も 激励し続けてくれた
Even on such cowardly days, you kept cheering me on,

198
00:39:16,494 --> 00:39:22,334
あなたに いつも感謝 転んでも 立ち上がる
always thanking you, getting back up even when I fall.

199
00:39:22,534 --> 00:39:28,814
夢を叶えたいんだ 必ず こんなにね 打ち込めるのは
I want to make my dreams come true, absolutely—the reason I can pour so much into this...

200
00:39:30,134 --> 00:39:35,694
そう 同志がいるから
That's right, because I have a comrade like you.

201
00:39:35,974 --> 00:39:41,954
あなたの悩みは 私が寄り添う
I will draw close to your worries.

202
00:39:42,194 --> 00:39:49,334
心が疲れたなら 休憩しよう 遠慮はしないで
If your heart gets tired, let's take a break, don't hold back.

203
00:39:50,334 --> 00:39:55,034
そんな仲じゃない 二人
We're not the kind of pair to hold back.

204
00:39:55,294 --> 00:40:00,034
二人 肩を 組んで ほら 何度でも 乗り越えるよ
Linking arms, see, we'll overcome anything over and over again.

205
00:40:00,580 --> 00:40:02,120
乗り越えるよ
We'll get through it...

206
00:40:02,660 --> 00:40:07,720
世界中が敵になっても
Even if the whole world turns against us,

207
00:40:09,240 --> 00:40:14,060
変わらずあなたの味方
I'll always be on your side.

208
00:40:14,640 --> 00:40:21,180
右と左 「友達の証だよ」って 強く
Right and left, saying 'It's proof we're friends,' strongly...

209
00:40:22,360 --> 00:40:27,700
固く キツく 縛ったリボン
Firmly and tightly tied with a ribbon.

210
00:40:28,440 --> 00:40:34,840
話題のドラマも 虹の出る空も
Even the talked-about dramas, even the skies where rainbows appear,

211
00:40:35,220 --> 00:40:41,640
掴み取る栄光も 一緒に見たい
And the glory we grasp, I want to see it together with you.

212
00:40:41,940 --> 00:40:54,340
あなたが笑えば 私もつられる 隣り合わせの心 連鎖してるよ
When you smile, I catch it too; our side-by-side hearts are linked together.

213
00:40:54,940 --> 00:41:01,800
いずれ それぞれの 道を歩いても 共に 支え
Even if we eventually walk our separate paths, let's support each other

214
00:41:02,140 --> 00:41:09,380
さあ 未来へと 進んで行こう
Now, let's advance forward into the future.

215
00:41:11,240 --> 00:41:16,760
どこにいても 二人三脚
No matter where we are, we're running side-by-side.

216
00:41:21,320 --> 00:41:30,640
with you...

217
00:41:44,048 --> 00:41:44,888
いぇーい！
Yay!

218
00:41:45,048 --> 00:41:45,608
凄い！
Amazing!

219
00:41:45,748 --> 00:41:46,628
素敵だ！
That's wonderful!

220
00:41:47,148 --> 00:41:48,048
二度目ですけど！？
This is our second time though?!

221
00:41:48,628 --> 00:41:50,328
忘れてたから！
Because I forgot!

222
00:41:51,608 --> 00:41:52,628
6周年！
6th anniversary!

223
00:41:52,808 --> 00:41:53,568
6！
Six!

224
00:41:53,748 --> 00:41:54,788
こっちで
Over here...

225
00:41:55,568 --> 00:41:57,368
こっちじゃないの？
Isn't it this way?

226
00:41:57,528 --> 00:41:58,528
こう？
Like this?

227
00:41:58,668 --> 00:41:59,468
韓国はこうだよ
In Korea, it's like this.

228
00:42:00,388 --> 00:42:01,648
勉強になりました、ありがとうございます！
I learned something new, thank you!

229
00:42:02,168 --> 00:42:03,088
6がこうなんだね。
So 6 is like this.

230
00:42:03,208 --> 00:42:03,808
6！
Six!

231
00:42:04,008 --> 00:42:04,568
おめでとう！
Congratulations!

232
00:42:04,688 --> 00:42:05,248
ありがとう！
Thank you!

233
00:42:05,388 --> 00:42:06,448
おめでとう！
Congratulations!

234
00:42:06,588 --> 00:42:07,728
ありがとう、嬉しい！
Thank you, I'm so happy!

235
00:42:07,868 --> 00:42:11,988
そうなんですよ、実はこの前ツナのね、はい。
That's right, actually just recently, Tsuna's... yeah.

236
00:42:12,148 --> 00:42:13,888
記念ライブ、誕生日ね？
Anniversary live, birthday right?

237
00:42:14,048 --> 00:42:17,648
誕生日記念のライブにね、出させていただいたのね！
We got to perform at your birthday anniversary live!

238
00:42:17,988 --> 00:42:19,248
今回は
And this time...

239
00:42:19,388 --> 00:42:21,168
え、なんかさ、初めてなんだよね？
Wait, isn't this your first time?

240
00:42:21,308 --> 00:42:24,208
そう！ホロライブのスタジオに来ましたー！
Yes! I came to the Hololive studio!

241
00:42:24,688 --> 00:42:25,828
めちゃくちゃ喜
We were so hap—

242
00:42:25,828 --> 00:42:26,808
やったー！
Yay!

243
00:42:27,128 --> 00:42:28,428
やったー！
Yay!

244
00:42:29,208 --> 00:42:31,168
え、すごい！え、すごい！
Oh, amazing! Oh, amazing!

245
00:42:33,708 --> 00:42:36,148
やったー！ありがとうございます！わざわざ来てくれて！
Yay! Thank you so much for coming all this way!

246
00:42:36,688 --> 00:42:38,548
もういっぱい吸っていきます！
I'm going to soak it all in!

247
00:42:38,768 --> 00:42:45,088
初めて、そう、ホロライブのスタジオで3Dでコラボしたの、ありがとう！
For the first time, doing a 3D collaboration in the Hololive studio, thank you!

248
00:42:45,608 --> 00:42:47,668
そしてなんと、2年ぶりですよ！
And what's more, it's been 2 years!

249
00:42:47,848 --> 00:42:48,668
そうなんだね！
Has it been!

250
00:42:48,828 --> 00:42:54,908
そう、この「二人三脚」っていう曲をね、やらせていただいたんですけれども、
Right, we performed this song called 'Futari Sankyaku',

251
00:42:55,468 --> 00:42:57,868
トワのファーストソロライブの時に初めてやって、覚えてた？フリ。
which we first did during Towa's first solo live. Did you remember the choreography?

252
00:42:58,048 --> 00:43:00,008
いやもう、完全に忘れてた！
No, I completely forgot!

253
00:43:02,068 --> 00:43:07,388
でも分かる、いろんなのやってくとね、こう忘れちゃうから。しかも2年ぶりだし。
But I get it, when you do a bunch of different things, you tend to forget. Plus it's been 2 years.

254
00:43:07,568 --> 00:43:10,828
そう、忘れちゃったけど、でもお前はさ、シークレットゲストだったじゃん。
Right, I forgot, but you were a secret guest.

255
00:43:11,228 --> 00:43:15,448
そしたらなんかサムネで私がいる！い るってなって！
And then I saw the thumbnail and went, 'I'm there! I'm there!'

256
00:43:15,788 --> 00:43:20,988
嬉しい！でも本当にね、あの、あの曲、あそこで終わりじゃなくてこうやってね、またできたのがすごい嬉しいので、
I'm so happy! And I'm really glad we were able to do that song again like this instead of it ending there,

257
00:43:21,264 --> 00:43:27,364
ありがとうございます！
Thank you so much!

258
00:43:27,364 --> 00:43:28,424
ありがとうございます！
Thank you!

259
00:43:28,864 --> 00:43:39,404
っていうことでね、なんかソロライブの時にコラボした後こうやって3Dでコラボすることなかったから、今日はみなさんに無料で今お届けしてるので！
So anyway, since we hadn't done a 3D collab since that solo live, today we're bringing it to everyone for free!

260
00:43:39,804 --> 00:43:41,204
無料でーす！
It's free!

261
00:43:41,784 --> 00:43:44,464
えっと、じゃあ、写真タイムするか？
Um, well then, should we do a photo time?

262
00:43:44,464 --> 00:43:45,224
